(7253792, 1126979, 103142, '<td valign="top">So sorry about the DQ! I won''t pick on the SC too much since I haven''t seen the original. However, it does seem a little over the top if I were to pick on the SC. :)<br/> <br/>Still, I''m so glad I don''t have to do the job. And you''ll ribbon again next time you enter anyway. Your creativity <b>always </b>astounds me! :D</td>', 'So sorry about the DQ! I won''t pick on the SC too much since I haven''t seen the original. However, it does seem a little over the top if I were to pick on the SC. :) Still, I''m so glad I don''t have to do the job. And you''ll ribbon again next time you enter anyway. Your creativity always astounds me! :D', '2014-08-22 12:52:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7254318, 1126976, 14476, '<td valign="top">GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB:<br/>After a long hiatus, I''m back working at the duties of the Critique Club, where we try to give an indepth review of the image randomly set before us.  If you find this review helpful, please tick the box that says so.  then the Critique Club members feel as if they are really helping!<br/> <br/>Okay, this image has a lot going for it, simply because it is original.<br/> <br/>Technically it has a bit of a problem, because I suspect the photographer wanted the b''ground to be solid black, but those unfortunate streaks to the right of the image worked against you for that effect.<br/> <br/>Now, a purist might argue that you''ve given your runner two knees, but without them, you would not have the motion effect.  So, that''s okay, and besides it works.<br/> <br/>What would really set this fun image apart would be if the stick figure were carrying something.  Preferably something bright red, to give a strong focal point.<br/> <br/>It''s a good image.  Personally, while voting, I gave it an 8, for originality.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work. <br/> <br/></td>', 'GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB:After a long hiatus, I''m back working at the duties of the Critique Club, where we try to give an indepth review of the image randomly set before us.  If you find this review helpful, please tick the box that says so.  then the Critique Club members feel as if they are really helping! Okay, this image has a lot going for it, simply because it is original. Technically it has a bit of a problem, because I suspect the photographer wanted the b''ground to be solid black, but those unfortunate streaks to the right of the image worked against you for that effect. Now, a purist might argue that you''ve given your runner two knees, but without them, you would not have the motion effect.  So, that''s okay, and besides it works. What would really set this fun image apart would be if the stick figure were carrying something.  Preferably something bright red, to give a strong focal point. It''s a good image.  Personally, while voting, I gave it an 8, for originality. Keep up the good work.  ', '2014-08-23 23:26:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7254344, 1127004, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Color Saturation &amp; Hue - Not Applicable.<br/> <br/>Brightness and contrast - the lighting seems a bit off to me.  I''m a big fan of inky velvet black, but their power doesn''t quite gather here.  Perhaps more than one light might have helped.  As is there are bright spots that fight with the piral for the eye''s attention.  I''m left wondering if the light following the spiral might have worked.<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field - excellent.  The image is tack sharp.  <br/> <br/>Subjective - I like the image, but find the lighting vs the shape a bit jarring.  A bit different lighting could have made this ominous, or another angle might have made it mysterious.  <br/> <br/>Overall, very daunting to try to critique an acknowledged master...</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Color Saturation & Hue - Not Applicable. Brightness and contrast - the lighting seems a bit off to me.  I''m a big fan of inky velvet black, but their power doesn''t quite gather here.  Perhaps more than one light might have helped.  As is there are bright spots that fight with the piral for the eye''s attention.  I''m left wondering if the light following the spiral might have worked. Focus and depth of field - excellent.  The image is tack sharp.   Subjective - I like the image, but find the lighting vs the shape a bit jarring.  A bit different lighting could have made this ominous, or another angle might have made it mysterious.   Overall, very daunting to try to critique an acknowledged master...', '2014-08-24 00:08:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7255048, 1126453, 119012, '<td valign="top">critique club:<br/> <br/>the problem i have with this image is i dont know what it is without reading your description, you also have some sharpening artifact going on and the toothpick edges are jagged and could use some anti aliasing.</td>', 'critique club: the problem i have with this image is i dont know what it is without reading your description, you also have some sharpening artifact going on and the toothpick edges are jagged and could use some anti aliasing.', '2014-08-25 13:08:16.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
